---
title: Orecchiette with turnip greens
category: Mains
cuisine: Italian
tags:
  - Italy
servings: 2
difficulty: easy
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
created: 2026-05-22
updated: 2026-05-22
---

Take @turnip greens{600%g}, discard the thick stems, and give them a good rinse.

Fill a #large pot{} with salted water and bring to boil. Add the turnip greens and cook for ~{5%minutes}.

Drizzle @olive oil{} into a #large pan{} and add @breadcrumbs{30%g}. Fry on medium until they turn a deep gold, then remove and set aside.

Add more oil to the pan and this time put in @garlic{1%clove}(crushed), @chili pepper{1}, and @anchovies{2}. Stir with a wooden spoon until the anchovies break apart and dissolve, then remove the garlic and chili pepper and turn off the heat.

Cook @orecchiette{200%g} in the pot together with the turnip greens. Mix them delicately every once in a while.

Once cooked, drain the orecchiette and turnip greens and turn them into the pan with the fried anchovies. Sauté for a minute and salt to taste.

> Remember the anchovies are already quite salty.

Sprinkle with the fried breadcrumbs and drizzle with olive oil before serving.